1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,487
A model is only as honest as the maps beneath it.

2
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:08,425
CoolSpend stands on four real, independently sourced layers of Barcelona.

3
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:15,787
The first is a satellite vulnerability grid: four hundred and ninety-four cells, each roughly four hundred metres across.

4
00:00:15,787 --> 00:00:18,987
Landsat reads land-surface temperature.

5
00:00:18,987 --> 00:00:22,950
Sentinel-one radar reads sealed, paved ground.

6
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:30,412
And Sentinel-two reads NDVI — a satellite greenness index, where low values mean little existing vegetation.

7
00:00:30,412 --> 00:00:34,625
Together they answer where to look — not how much a plan will cool.

8
00:00:34,625 --> 00:00:42,650
Second, OpenStreetMap gives real building, road and street-furniture geometry, so no tree lands on a roof or in traffic.

9
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:49,100
Third, Barcelona's arbrat-viari street-tree inventory supplies a twelve-species candidate table.

10
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:58,737
And fourth, the Padró municipal register: one million, seven hundred and two thousand, eight hundred and fourteen residents, across seventy-three neighbourhoods.

11
00:00:58,737 --> 00:01:00,375
Four maps.

12
00:01:00,375 --> 00:01:02,262
One real city.

